# What EAS Build may NOT upload.
#
# THIS FILE HAS TO BE AT THE REPOSITORY ROOT, not next to eas.json.
#
# `eas build` with EAS_NO_VCS=1 archives from the repository root, so a
# .easignore inside driver-app/ is read too late to exclude anything above it.
# The first attempts uploaded a 1,020 MB archive that included .runtime/ - the
# local Postgres data directory, the demo server logs, and the synthetic login
# files. That is why this file exists at this level.
#
# EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, DELIBERATELY.
#
# These are gitignore patterns: an unanchored `i18n/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth. The first version of this file wrote `i18n/`, meaning
# the repo's translation directory, and it also excluded
# `driver-app/src/i18n/` - so the build got all the way to Metro and failed
# with "Unable to resolve module ../i18n/language". A leading slash pins each
# pattern to the repository root, which is what was meant every time.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the archive; it does not add to it. So
# every exclusion has to be named here, including the obvious ones.

# Archive inspection for Terrain Command found agent chat exports, telemetry,
# local tool configuration and memory files outside the Expo app were still
# included. This app has no workspace dependencies: allow only its directory
# at the repository root, including when new local tooling folders appear.
/*
# NO TRAILING SLASH ON THIS NEGATION, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE BUG.
#
# `/*` ignores the `driver-app` DIRECTORY ENTRY itself. A negation written
# `!/driver-app/` only ever matches a path spelled with a trailing slash, so the
# directory entry stayed ignored, the archiver pruned it without descending, and
# EAS uploaded an 80-BYTE archive - build 6c856cb0 died in 6.5 s with
# "Unknown error. See logs of the Build complete hook".
#
# Adding `!/driver-app/**` does NOT rescue it: the parent directory node is
# still ignored, so the walker never reaches anything to re-include.
# Reproduced against the same `ignore` npm package the archiver uses.
!/driver-app

# The local demo runtime: Postgres data and binaries, server logs, and the
# synthetic account files. None of it builds anything and none of it may leave
# this machine.
/.runtime/
/logs/

# Nothing outside the Expo app is needed to build the Expo app.
/backend/
/ml/
/data/
/design-system/
/manager-web/
/tests/
/docs/
/i18n/
/.github/
/.git/

# Dependencies and build output. The EAS builder installs its own.
node_modules/
/driver-app/.expo/
/driver-app/dist/
/driver-app/web-build/
/driver-app/android/
/driver-app/ios/

# Credentials and keys, restated rather than inherited.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account*.json
secrets/
*.log
*.db
*.sqlite*
